--- A program calling magpie's `backup` alone lowers, in both modes: the
--- module's `_fixed`, which the program does not call, had an answer of no
--- value in an early round (its first return an error), which was joined
--- with the local it returns — its parameter `by` — and written back to
--- the parameter, so the lowered program disagreed with itself; and the
--- sequencer's `put_rows`, not called either, hands `revise` a function
--- its own untyped parameter cannot type, which had been refused as the
--- program's mistake (crow check --self: magpie.backup).
use magpie

r = magpie.backup['no-such-log', 'no-such-backup']
log[r.ok]
log[len[r.reason] gt 0]
